; Vendored, not scanned as first-party: dune builds these without applying this
; project's warning settings, and their own tests are not ours to run.
;
; [ocaml-model-explorer] carries its own [model-explorer] gitlink, which stays
; uninitialised on purpose -- it is the upstream TypeScript renderer, fetched
; from npm at the pinned version rather than built from source here.
;
; [err_trace] (module [Err]) is not vendored: it is the opam package, and
; melange builds use its [err_trace-melange] library.
;
; [bytesrw] is NOT built by dune at all -- it carries no dune files (upstream
; ships a topkg/ocamlbuild build), and this project consumes the real opam
; package, unpatched (see .ai/model_explorer_design.md and
; lib/model_explorer_export/me_export.ml's [encode_bounded] for why: the
; installed `jsont` package is a fixed transitive consumer of bytesrw, and
; this devcontainer's opam switch is read-only to this process, so there is
; no way to rebuild it against a local patch here). This checkout exists
; purely as a carrier for that patch -- a submodule pointing at
; github.com/TheCBaH/bytesrw, a fork of github.com/dbuenzli/bytesrw -- kept
; out of @fmt/@all the same way the others above are, since none of its
; ~60 files are ours to reformat or build.

(vendored_dirs ocaml-yamlt opickle ocaml-model-explorer bytesrw)
